flowchart TB
    accTitle: The checks of this website
    accDescr: scripts/check.sh runs scripts/check-project.sh last, with the three checks of this website: the tests of its scripts, the tables of the projects of projects.toml in README.md and README.de.md and the tests of its hooks. When one fails, the PR coach explains it in the words of .github/checks.project.toml. A table that differs fixes itself: the job of the check runs .github/mkdocs_project.py --write, the fix bot commits the READMEs onto the branch of the pull request, and the checks run again; on a pull request from a fork, a person runs that command and pushes. A test that fails, or a line that no test runs, needs a person, who fixes the code or its test and pushes.

    pull(["A pull request"])
    script["scripts/check-project.sh"]
    scripts["Tests of the scripts<br>of the website"]
    table["The projects of projects.toml<br>in the READMEs"]
    hooks["Tests of the hooks<br>of the website"]
    coach["The PR coach explains it<br>from .github/checks.project.toml"]
    write[".github/mkdocs_project.py<br>--write"]
    bot["The fix bot commits the READMEs<br>onto a branch of this repository"]
    person(["A person fixes the code<br>or its test and pushes"])

    pull --> script
    script --> scripts & table & hooks
    scripts & table & hooks -- "fails" --> coach
    coach -- "the table differs" --> write
    write --> bot
    bot -. "the checks run again" .-> script
    coach -- "a test fails" --> person
    person -.-> pull

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    class script,scripts,table,hooks,coach,write,bot bot
    class person person
